  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Working Type Specimen",
    "overview": "The portfolio is set like a foundry's specimen book. Every section is a specimen page: a huge setting of one word or name, the measurements of that setting printed beside it in mono, and hairline rules dividing the page into ruled lines rather than boxes. The visitor is not told about craft; they see a face set at size with its size, leading, weight and width annotated, and they can change it.\n\nDensity is editorial and generous at the top of each page, then tight and ruled below: lists of projects, jobs, testimonials and facts sit between full-width black hairlines, never in cards. One variable family (Archivo, weight 100 to 900, width 62 to 125) carries every voice; contrast comes from moving its axes, not from adding faces. Martian Mono is the specimen's furniture: metrics, dates, counts, running heads. Measurement blue is the printer's correction pen, kept for metrics, baselines, selection and the single most important action.\n\nThe only rounded, shadowed object in the world is the Figma-style fonts panel, deliberately kept as a piece of software laid on the specimen page. The world rejects the category default of a short headline over a grid of equal thumbnail cards.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White coated paper, black ink, warm grey stock bands, one blue.",
      "One variable sans (Archivo) at many widths and weights; Martian Mono only for measurements and page furniture.",
      "Display settings fill the measure, run between dashed blue baselines, and are annotated live.",
      "Structure by full-width hairline rules; no cards, no shadows, square corners everywhere outside the fonts panel.",
      "Motion is axis interpolation: width and weight ease over 320ms."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Measuring Pen Rule",
        "body": "Blue marks measurements, baselines, selection, focus and the one lead action. It is never a background band, never body text, and never a second decorative accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Inks Rule",
        "body": "Running text and headings are ink or grey ink; colour on text is reserved for measurements, link hover and before/after markers. Hierarchy comes from size, weight and width, not from tinting text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule",
        "body": "Archivo carries every voice. Make contrast by moving weight and width, not by introducing another face. The fonts panel may set the title in other faces because that is its job; nothing else does.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Annotated Setting Rule",
        "body": "A display setting is accompanied by its measurements in blue mono (face, size/leading, weight, width, tracking), and those numbers must be true of the setting as rendered.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Measures Rule",
        "body": "Martian Mono appears only for numbers, measurements, dates and page furniture. Never for headings, sentences or buttons with words.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Printed Page Rule",
        "body": "Outside the fonts panel there are no shadows and no raised surfaces. If something needs separation, give it a rule or a stock band.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do set display type to fill the column and annotate it with true measurements in blue Martian Mono.",
      "Do make hierarchy with Archivo's weight and width axes; condensed heads (width 88 to 90), light condensed figures (300, width 75).",
      "Do divide content with full-width 1px black rules, and use hairline grey only for subdivisions inside a ruled block.",
      "Do mat every screenshot on warm stock with no border or radius.",
      "Do animate only axes (width, weight) and ink inversion, over 320ms with `cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)`; respect reduced motion.",
      "Do keep every role working in both themes; the dark theme is a value swap, not a new layout."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use cards, rounded boxes or shadows anywhere except the fonts panel.",
      "Don't use measurement blue as a band, a body-text colour or a decorative accent; one blue-filled lead action per band at most.",
      "Don't introduce a second text family; other faces appear only as samples inside the fonts panel.",
      "Don't use Martian Mono for sentences, headings or uppercase labels above headings.",
      "Don't lay projects out as a grid of equal thumbnail cards.",
      "Don't use terracotta outside a before/after comparison."
    ]
  }
}